 "tags": "triceratops dinosaur three horns frill herbivore prehistoric reptile quadruped",
 "review": {
  "score": 8.0,
  "round": 1,
  "problems": [
   "Scale: in the beside-a-person frame the back only reaches the man's chest and the frill top is at shoulder height. A real triceratops is about 3 m tall at the frill and about twice a person's height, so here it reads more like a calf than an adult.",
   "The frill is a plain flat brown oval with a brass rim. It reads a little like a separate disc stuck behind the head, because nothing ties it to the neck or gives it a bony edge. It still reads as a frill, just not as solidly as it could.",
   "The nose horn (poly 203,-160 / 222,-166 / 224,-202) is small and gets lost against the long brow horns. That weakens the 'three horns' read at small size.",
   "The far legs have no toenail dots while the near legs do. This is fine for depth, but in the walking frames the far front leg (legA at 70,-140) disappears behind the near one."
  ]
 },
 "for": "a big three-horned plant-eating dinosaur with a bony neck frill, walking on four thick legs",
 "source": "minted",
 "created": "2026-11-02",
 "sprite": {
  "w": 998.4,
  "h": 611.0,
  "ax": 0.5,
  "ay": 0.97,
  "src": "mg/library/mint/sprites/triceratops.png"
 },
 "sprite_review": {
  "score": 6.0,
  "problems": [
   "Scale: in the 'beside a person' frame the triceratops is shorter than the man. The top of its frill only reaches about his chest and its back is around his hip. A real triceratops stands about 3 m at the hips with a 9 m body, so it should be well over head height and several people long. At this size it reads as a pony-sized toy dinosaur.",
   "Style: the skin has detailed painterly texture and slightly realistic shading, which is busier than the house look of clean, flat shading. The blue-grey and tan colours are acceptable for an animal that needs its own colour.",
   "Minor: the frill-edge knobs and the toe claws are bright white dots that stand out more than the gold or brushed-metal highlights used elsewhere."
  ]
 }
}